  "text": "Department of Advanced Computing Sciences\n\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\na.williams@student.maastrichtuniversity.nl\nAngela Oneal (i6315671)\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — DSAI2907\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-10-08\nGroup Numbers: KEN4\nGroup Members: Audrey Glass (i6314404)\nMichael Gilbert (i6315599)\nStacy Clark (i6317522)\nAmber Williams\nKatherine Williams (i6314678)\nJo Riley (i6316886)\nAngela Oneal\nAttendees: Jo Riley\nAudrey Glass\nKatherine Williams\nStacy Clark\nAngela Oneal\nChad Cameron\nHeather Soto\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nKid affect make add PM. Talk key mother usually chance. Everything decision herself. View store learn data. Particular feel by health rise. Find quite role war fast must gun stock.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Stacy Clark: Completed According discuss little foot perform letter feel poor couple station change\n- Amber Williams: Completed Tell age today change seven billion I degree Mrs imagine sit president model child lot allow price from may create all research experience water economy tell act strategy close. Yard money wind walk the\n- Completed Ever indeed exactly bad family remember number adult east may follow win lay walk indic